# 2. Research: The recovery technologies we should use

There is an important distinction between restoring a file from trash and recovering permanently deleted storage data.

These are different engineering problems.



### Recovery technology stack

| Technology | Purpose | Priority |
|---|---|---|
| MediaStore Trash | Restore trashed media | Critical |
| Android 16+ deleted-file APIs | Discover tracked deleted external media where supported | Critical |
| Storage Access Framework | User-authorized access to folders and SD cards | Critical |
| File Signature Carving | Identify recoverable file structures | Advanced |
| JPEG/PNG/HEIC parsing | Validate image structures | High |
| MP4/MOV parsing | Validate video structures | High |
| EXIF metadata analysis | Identify image metadata | High |
| Thumbnail analysis | Discover surviving image previews | High |
| Filesystem analysis | Identify filesystem metadata where permitted | Advanced |
| SHA-256 verification | Verify recovered file integrity | Critical |
| FFmpeg/Media parsing | Validate media streams | Advanced |

Useful research references:

- [Android MediaStore API](https://developer.android.com/reference/android/provider/MediaStore?utm_source=chatgpt.com)
- [Android Scoped Storage](https://source.android.com/docs/core/storage/scoped?utm_source=chatgpt.com)
- [Android Media Access Guide](https://developer.android.com/training/data-storage/shared/media?utm_source=chatgpt.com)
- [Android Storage Access Framework](https://developer.android.com/training/data-storage/shared/documents-files?authuser=111&utm_source=chatgpt.com)

**Important technical limitation:** Android does not allow an ordinary application to freely read raw internal storage partitions. On modern encrypted Android devices, permanently deleted data may be inaccessible because of filesystem restrictions, encryption and storage TRIM.

No algorithm, AI model or machine-learning system can reconstruct file contents that no longer exist in accessible storage.

We should maximize legitimate recovery opportunities without making false recovery promises.

